<area shape="rect" id="node5" title="ddd.models.objects.A2lObjectOptions

What a declaration asks of the a2l backend. Only that backend interprets it.

Nothing here changes the generated c or the meaning of the object; a project that
generates no a2l can leave the whole block out.
" alt="" coords="1141,666,1378,778"/>
<area shape="rect" id="node6" title="ddd.models.objects.Limits

Physical lower/upper limit of a data object.
" alt="" coords="1175,533,1344,617"/>
<area shape="rect" id="node7" title="ddd.models.types.Member

One member of a structure, in the order the structure declares it.

Order is significant: it is the order the c struct is generated in, and therefore the order
the compiler lays out. &#160;Reordering members of a released structure moves every address after
the change, which is why a comparison against a baseline reports it.
" alt="" coords="383,119,983,455"/>
<area shape="rect" id="node8" title="ddd.models.types.StructType

One structured datatype: a name and the members it lays out, in order.
" alt="" coords="5,5,239,145"/>
